WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:30.625
<b>Here,</b>

2
00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:32.083
<b>Lord Krishna explains</b>

3
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:38.875
<b>that just as strong winds can pull away </b>
<b>a boat floating on water with their force,</b>

4
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:40.000
<b>similarly,</b>

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.166
<b>the senses chasing pleasures</b>
<b>pull away one's wisdom.</b>

6
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:52.250
<b>Think about this</b>

7
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:56.791
<b>- if a boatman doesn't maintain </b>
<b>control over their boat,</b>

8
00:00:56.791 --> 00:01:03.500
<b>the forceful winds will carry it away, </b>
<b>causing it to drift.</b>

9
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.291
<b>Therefore,</b>

10
00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:06.375
<b>to reach one's destination,</b>

11
00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:12.458
<b>it's essential that a boatman maintains </b>
<b>complete control over the boat.</b>

12
00:01:12.458 --> 00:01:14.375
<b>Without control,</b>

13
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:17.583
<b>the mind too is like such a boat,</b>

14
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:21.833
<b>surrounded by countless objects </b>
<b>of sensory attraction.</b>

15
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:26.791
<b>The senses constantly pull toward these objects,</b>
<b>flowing with them,</b>

16
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:31.166
<b>and in doing so, they carry away the </b>
<b>boat-like mind with them,</b>

17
00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:32.916
<b>causing it to wander.</b>

18
00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:34.541
<b>And when the mind wanders,</b>

19
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:37.958
<b>a person's inner balance disturbs,</b>

20
00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:41.083
<b>wisdom becomes unstable.</b>

21
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.708
<b>For example</b>

22
00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.166
<b>- you're busy with some work,</b>

23
00:01:45.166 --> 00:01:50.208
<b>and suddenly your favorite song's </b>
<b>tune reaches your ears.</b>

24
00:01:50.208 --> 00:01:54.958
<b>First, your attention will go toward </b>
<b>determining if it's indeed that song,</b>

25
00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:58.083
<b>and where this tune is coming from.</b>

26
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:02.041
<b>The tune is coming from afar, not clearly audible,</b>

27
00:02:02.041 --> 00:02:05.958
<b>so perhaps now you'll desire to listen to that song,</b>

28
00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.125
<b>to watch its video.</b>

29
00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:11.666
<b>You thought it's just a matter of moments,</b>

30
00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:15.500
<b>but then before you know it, </b>
<b>one song leads to another,</b>

31
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.083
<b>some old memories</b>

32
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:20.375
<b>other thoughts arise, </b>
<b>and the mind has wandered off,</b>

33
00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:22.625
<b>leaving work incomplete.</b>

34
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:25.750
<b>Doesn't this happen with you too?</b>

35
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>Here, Lord Krishna</b>

36
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.625
<b>is cautioning us about the adverse effects </b>
<b>of wandering senses on an uncontrolled mind. </b>

37
00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:39.958
<b>He's trying to help us understand that we </b>
<b>shouldn't underestimate the power of the senses </b>

38
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:42.583
<b>- if the mind remains uncontrolled,</b>

39
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:48.791
<b>even a single sense is capable of </b>
<b>causing it to stray from its purpose.</b>

40
00:02:48.791 --> 00:02:55.583
<b>Just as a boatman must maintain control over </b>
<b>the boat to protect against the wind's force,</b>

41
00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:58.666
<b>constantly rowing their oars,</b>

42
00:02:58.666 --> 00:02:59.958
<b>similarly,</b>

43
00:02:59.958 --> 00:03:03.208
<b>a person must keep their mind under control,</b>

44
00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:05.291
<b>steadily performing their duties.</b>

45
00:03:09.625 --> 00:03:12.458
<b>For success in life,</b>

46
00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:18.041
<b>you must learn to focus your</b>
<b>attention solely on your goal.</b>

47
00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:25.833
<b>This requires developing the ability</b>
<b>to disregard sensory distractions.</b>

48
00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:27.291
<b>Otherwise,</b>

49
00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:33.708
<b>these will disturb your mind </b>
<b>and divert your attention.</b>

50
00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:39.083
<b>The senses are perpetually searching</b>
<b>for some object of desire.</b>

51
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:42.875
<b>They constantly seek beautiful sights,</b>

52
00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:44.416
<b>pleasant fragrances,</b>

53
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:48.500
<b>exquisite tastes, and so forth.</b>

54
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:56.333
<b>Yet they cannot compel </b>
<b>you against your willpower.</b>

55
00:03:56.333 --> 00:04:02.000
<b>While senses can certainly bring signals </b>
<b>of objects to your attention,</b>

56
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:10.250
<b>sometimes even persisting</b>
<b>stubbornly on one thing,</b>

57
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.458
<b>ultimately,</b>

58
00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:20.125
<b>only the mind holds the privilege </b>
<b>to respond to these signals.</b>

59
00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:25.375
<b>If the mind hears these sensory signals </b>
<b>yet chooses to ignore them,</b>

60
00:04:25.375 --> 00:04:28.666
<b>its focus remains unbroken.</b>

61
00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:35.375
<b>But if the mind shows too</b>
<b>much interest in that signal,</b>

62
00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:40.750
<b>the senses will cleverly lead it astray.</b>

63
00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:45.291
<b>A simple signal transforms into an experience, </b>

64
00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:49.166
<b>experience morphs into desire,</b>

65
00:04:49.166 --> 00:04:59.041
<b>and desire quickly intensifies into craving. </b>
<b>Then distraction becomes inevitable.</b>

66
00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:01.958
<b>Understand it this way</b>

67
00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:04.750
<b>- the mind is like a king</b>

68
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:08.083
<b>with 5 ministers in his court.</b>

69
00:05:08.083 --> 00:05:09.791
<b>All five are clever.</b>

70
00:05:09.791 --> 00:05:11.875
<b>All five compete.</b>

71
00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:14.708
<b>They offer different suggestions to the king</b>

72
00:05:14.708 --> 00:05:20.125
<b>and want the king to follow their advice alone.</b>

73
00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:23.000
<b>What should the king do?  </b>

74
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.125
<b>If the king is foolish,</b>

75
00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:28.458
<b>he'll try to follow everyone's suggestions,</b>

76
00:05:28.458 --> 00:05:30.166
<b>and the clever ministers</b>

77
00:05:30.166 --> 00:05:34.875
<b>will entangle him in their eloquence.</b>

78
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:37.458
<b>But if the king is wise,</b>

79
00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:40.625
<b>he'll listen to all suggestions</b>

80
00:05:40.625 --> 00:05:45.416
<b>yet do what he deems right,</b>

81
00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:48.875
<b>what serves his purpose.</b>

82
00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:55.875
<b>First and foremost, this requires </b>
<b>having a defined goal.</b>

83
00:05:55.875 --> 00:06:00.666
<b>This defined goal is crucial in life</b>

84
00:06:00.666 --> 00:06:08.291
<b>- it's the scale on which you weigh </b>
<b>what's important and what isn't.</b>

85
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:14.791
<b>When to ignore the senses, when to utilize them.</b>

86
00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:18.791
<b>Don't get caught in the eloquence of the senses;</b>

87
00:06:18.791 --> 00:06:27.875
<b>you don't serve them, you use them </b>
<b>to manage your life's kingdom.</b>

88
00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:30.583
<b>Be a wise king.</b>

89
00:06:35.458 --> 00:06:42.750
<b>The original purpose of the senses </b>
<b>was merely to assist in living life,</b>

90
00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.791
<b>but</b>

91
00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:45.791
<b>in today's environment,</b>

92
00:06:45.791 --> 00:06:53.000
<b>people have become slaves to their </b>
<b>senses rather than using them.</b>

93
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.583
<b>Sensory indulgence has become </b>
<b>a standard of prestige.</b>

94
00:06:58.583 --> 00:07:01.125
<b>Who has the bigger vehicle,</b>

95
00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:03.916
<b>whose clothes are more beautiful,</b>

96
00:07:03.916 --> 00:07:06.875
<b>who's traveling abroad,</b>

97
00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:09.708
<b>who watched that popular series</b>

98
00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:14.083
<b>and who's falling behind in all this?</b>

99
00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:19.208
<b>You must have heard many such examples.</b>

100
00:07:19.208 --> 00:07:20.291
<b>Perhaps</b>

101
00:07:20.291 --> 00:07:28.666
<b>you too have participated</b>
<b>in such comparative thoughts.</b>

102
00:07:28.666 --> 00:07:30.625
<b>Now tell me,</b>

103
00:07:30.625 --> 00:07:36.166
<b>when did you last hear these questions?</b>

104
00:07:36.166 --> 00:07:38.541
<b>Who is content?</b>

105
00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:41.000
<b>Who is peaceful?</b>

106
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:48.541
<b>Who is progressing toward </b>
<b>their goal without ego?</b>

107
00:07:48.541 --> 00:07:53.125
<b>Society is merely a collection of individuals.</b>

108
00:07:53.125 --> 00:07:59.166
<b>It has no expression of its own.</b>

109
00:07:59.166 --> 00:08:02.541
<b>So who must change?</b>

110
00:08:02.541 --> 00:08:04.416
<b>You.</b>

111
00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:08.625
<b>Who must avoid straying?</b>

112
00:08:08.625 --> 00:08:09.916
<b>- You.</b>

113
00:08:09.916 --> 00:08:14.250
<b>Instead of making sensory </b>
<b>pleasures life's measure,</b>

114
00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:20.916
<b>you must make spiritual progress your purpose.</b>

115
00:08:20.916 --> 00:08:26.833
<b>Only then will society feel a positive impact.</b>

116
00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:35.291
<b>Where you focus your attention</b>

117
00:08:35.291 --> 00:08:41.500
<b>determines what results you'll achieve.</b>

118
00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:46.583
<b>In any organization,</b>
<b>you'll find two types of people:</b>

119
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:56.291
<b>Those who constantly focus on </b>
<b>unnecessary gossip and internal politics.</b>

120
00:08:56.291 --> 00:09:01.416
<b>They have every piece of related news.</b>

121
00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:06.083
<b>You surely know such people.</b>

122
00:09:06.083 --> 00:09:07.625
<b>Then</b>

123
00:09:07.625 --> 00:09:15.125
<b>there are others who focus solely on their work.</b>

124
00:09:15.125 --> 00:09:17.583
<b>Surprisingly,</b>

125
00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:24.875
<b>despite being in the same organization, </b>
<b>amid the same events and colleagues,</b>

126
00:09:24.875 --> 00:09:32.500
<b>they remain unaware of any gossip or politics.</b>

127
00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.791
<b>If the environment is the same,</b>

128
00:09:35.791 --> 00:09:41.375
<b>why this difference between </b>
<b>the two types of people?</b>

129
00:09:41.375 --> 00:09:42.708
<b>Simple.</b>

130
00:09:42.708 --> 00:09:45.166
<b>One focuses on work,</b>

131
00:09:45.166 --> 00:09:47.541
<b>on their goal.</b>

132
00:09:47.541 --> 00:09:50.458
<b>The other focuses on others.</b>

133
00:09:50.458 --> 00:09:54.125
<b>On goal or on others?</b>

134
00:09:54.125 --> 00:10:03.125
<b>Do you need to be told where to focus?</b>

135
00:10:03.125 --> 00:10:06.750
<b>You're wise enough to know.</b>

